WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.212 --> 00:00:00.920
MYLES BORINS: Hi.

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:02.696
I'm Myles Borins,
developer advocate

00:00:02.696 --> 00:00:04.070
for Google Cloud
Platform and one

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.560
of the maintainers of Node.js.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.760
I hear you're interested
in deploying a Node.js

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.447
application, so I
want to introduce you

00:00:09.447 --> 00:00:11.780
to an amazing product offering
available on Google Cloud

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.000
Platform.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.260
Node.js on App Engine
Standard is a great way

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.020
to quickly get your application
or service into the cloud.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.540
Take your Node project,
sprinkle a little bit of YAML,

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.050
run the magic command,
Gcloud App Deploy,

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.140
and you're ready to go.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.240
To demonstrate just how quickly
you can get your code up

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.500
and running, I'm
going to highlight

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.624
some of my favorite features
of App Engine Standard

00:00:29.624 --> 00:00:30.620
while deploying.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.889
So here we have
our package.json.

00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:34.430
It's for our Hello
World application.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.790
You could see that our
only dependency is express.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.330
Here is the server.js file.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:42.470
We create a single route that
always responds, Hello Node.js,

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.540
and we listen on
the default port.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.020
Last but not least, we sprinkle
a tiny bit of YAML to taste.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.410
The only thing remaining is to
run the magic command, Gcloud

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.430
App Deploy.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:58.016
So let's a the terminal up,
and a timer, and let's go.

00:00:58.016 --> 00:01:00.390
First off, you're going to
notice that the code you write

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.200
is idiomatic.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.480
There's nothing special or
magic about writing code

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.685
for App Engine.

00:01:04.685 --> 00:01:06.810
One of my favorite features
for App Engine Standard

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:07.890
is scale to zero.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.350
You only pay for
the compute you use.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.670
We manage the runtime for you.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.320
When the operating system
or node get an update,

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.130
you're going to get
it automagically.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.650
We also install all
the dependencies

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.397
in the cloud for you
prior to deployment,

00:01:18.397 --> 00:01:20.730
so you can be guaranteed that
your application's running

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.170
in a safe sandbox.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.870
Logging, introspection,
live debugging, monitoring--

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.010
you get all of that
out-of-the-box.

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.290
Want HTTPS?

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:28.847
We got you.

00:01:28.847 --> 00:01:30.930
We automate the process
of generating certificates

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.540
for default or custom domains.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.800
Well, looks like our
app is already deployed,

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.860
so let's pop open a
browser and take a look.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:44.050
So there you have it, deploying
Node.js to App Engine Standard

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.880
with just three magic words--

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.068
Gcloud App Deploy.

00:01:48.068 --> 00:01:50.410
[CHEERS]

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.650
Thanks for joining us today.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:52.372
I'm Myles Borins.

00:01:52.372 --> 00:01:54.580
Please feel free to post
any questions in the comment

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.770
section, or ping me on
Twitter at @MylesBorins.

